{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"R-29:2\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"29:2–3 treat “we believe” as a claim tested by affliction, then distinguish those who spoke truth; this makes the focus’s faith and mutual patience audible under pressure.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"29:2\",\"ar\":\"ءَامَنَّا وَهُمْ لَا يُفْتَنُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"29:3\",\"ar\":\"فَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِينَ صَدَقُوا۟\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus names belief and closes with reciprocal counsel in patience.\",\"limits\":\"These verses describe testing and truthful belief, but do not mention mutual counsel.\" ,\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-29:7\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The matching faith-and-righteous-deeds formula is followed by forgiveness and reward, giving the focus’s excepted group an explicit outcome parallel.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"29:7\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ لَنُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّـَٔاتِهِمْ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus uses the same two predicates to begin its exception.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not add mutual truth or patience.\" ,\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-29:9\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The faith-and-deeds profile in 29:9 is followed by a scene where some people’s claim to faith buckles when they are harmed; the nearby contrast makes endurance a test of the profile.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"29:9\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"},{\"ref\":\"29:10\",\"ar\":\"فَإِذَآ أُوذِىَ فِى ٱللَّهِ جَعَلَ فِتْنَةَ ٱلنَّاسِ كَعَذَابِ ٱللَّهِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus places mutual patience after faith and righteous deeds.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not identify the people in 29:10 with those in 29:9, or mention reciprocal counsel.\" ,\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-29:30\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The plea for help against a people characterized as corrupters gives a collective social counterpoint to the focus’s righteous deeds and shared moral practice.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"29:30\",\"ar\":\"ٱنصُرْنِى عَلَى ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلْمُفْسِدِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus defines its exception as a plural group with righteous deeds and mutual counsel.\",\"limits\":\"This is a broad ethical contrast; the verse does not name faith, truth, or patience.\" ,\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-29:36\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"Shuʿayb’s public appeal to worship, hope in the Last Day, and avoid corruption is rejected; it may sharpen the contrast between a refused prophetic address and the focus’s reciprocal truth-bearing community.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"29:36\",\"ar\":\"ٱعْبُدُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَٱرْجُوا۟ ٱلْيَوْمَ ٱلْءَاخِرَ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"29:37\",\"ar\":\"فَكَذَّبُوهُ\"}],\"missing\":\"The passage does not connect this rejected address to reciprocal counsel; another passage linking the prophetic call against فساد to a community’s mutual guidance could establish the comparison.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-29:41\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-29:44\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"Creation “in truth” for believers is followed by recitation and prayer that restrains indecency; this sequence could place mutual counsel in truth within a wider movement from truth to ethical practice.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"29:44\",\"ar\":\"خَلَقَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضَ بِٱلْحَقِّ\"},{\"ref\":\"29:45\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ تَنْهَىٰ عَنِ ٱلْفَحْشَآءِ وَٱلْمُنكَرِ\"}],\"missing\":\"Here بِٱلْحَقِّ describes creation, while the focus makes الحق the content of mutual counsel. A Quranic passage joining these senses directly could decide whether the sequence gives the focus’s counsel a cosmic grounding.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-29:58\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The same faith-and-deeds formula leads here to lasting rooms in Paradise, an outcome parallel to the focus’s exception from loss.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"29:58\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ لَنُبَوِّئَنَّهُم مِّنَ ٱلْجَنَّةِ غُرَفًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus begins its saved group with the identical paired predicates.\",\"limits\":\"The reward passage does not include mutual truth or patience in its stated conditions.\" ,\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-29:59\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"After the matching faith-and-deeds formula, 29:59 names patient people who rely on their Lord; patience is thus a defining practice of the rewarded group, not just a quality mentioned in passing.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"29:58\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"},{\"ref\":\"29:59\",\"ar\":\"ٱلَّذِينَ صَبَرُوا۟ وَعَلَىٰ رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus adds reciprocal patience to the same faith-and-deeds profile.\",\"limits\":\"This passage names patience and reliance, but does not say that believers counsel one another.\" ,\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-30:15\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The formula of belief and righteous deeds recurs as one side of the division on the Day the Hour rises, with delight as its outcome.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"30:15\",\"ar\":\"فَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ فَهُمْ فِى رَوْضَةٍۢ يُحْبَرُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus uses the same formula to identify those exempt from the human-loss verdict.\",\"limits\":\"The verse adds no counterpart to the focus’s two mutual-counsel clauses.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-30:44\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"30:44 says the one who does good prepares for their own selves, while the focus’s final predicates make the saved profile explicitly reciprocal as well as action-based.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"30:44\",\"ar\":\"وَمَنْ عَمِلَ صَٰلِحًۭا فَلِأَنفُسِهِمْ يَمْهَدُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"30:45\",\"ar\":\"لِيَجْزِىَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages foreground righteous action, but the focus adds mutual counsel to its profile.\",\"limits\":\"The verses do not oppose personal benefit to communal practice; the difference is one of emphasis.\" ,\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-30:45\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Believers and doers of righteous deeds are named as recipients of reward from God’s grace, a direct first-half profile parallel.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"30:45\",\"ar\":\"ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ مِن فَضْلِهِۦٓ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus begins its exception with the same belief-and-deeds pairing.\",\"limits\":\"This verse does not mention mutual truth or patience.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-30:60\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Here patience is commanded directly beside the assertion that God’s promise is true; the focus brings the same two themes together as what believers mutually counsel.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"30:60\",\"ar\":\"فَٱصْبِرْ إِنَّ وَعْدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقٌّۭ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus closes with بِٱلْحَقِّ and بِٱلصَّبْرِ, in the reverse order.\",\"limits\":\"30:60 addresses one person with an imperative and does not use the reciprocal verb تَوَاصَوْا۟.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-31:8\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The familiar faith-and-deeds pair appears as the condition for gardens of bliss, another explicit outcome parallel to the exception.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"31:8\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ لَهُمْ جَنَّٰتُ ٱلنَّعِيمِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Those are the focus’s first two predicates.\",\"limits\":\"The reward statement does not include mutual counsel.\" ,\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-31:9\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"After the faith-and-deeds promise, the reward is called God’s true promise; this may let the focus’s mutual counsel in الحق resonate with trust in a promise that is حقًّا.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"31:8\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"},{\"ref\":\"31:9\",\"ar\":\"وَعْدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقًّۭا\"}],\"missing\":\"In 31:9 حق describes the truth of God’s promise, not the content of counsel. A Quranic passage explicitly joining that promise with mutual exhortation could establish the proposed relation.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-31:14\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The same وصي root appears in God’s charge to humanity concerning parents, while the focus uses the reciprocal form تَوَاصَوْا۟ for believers’ charge to one another; the family passage adds gratitude and care as another field of transmitted duty.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"31:14\",\"ar\":\"وَوَصَّيْنَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ بِوَٰلِدَيْهِ\"},{\"ref\":\"31:15\",\"ar\":\"وَصَاحِبْهُمَا فِى ٱلدُّنْيَا مَعْرُوفًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s repeated mutual verb invites comparison with this distinct form of charging and its following instruction about companionship.\",\"limits\":\"The forms and relations differ: 31:14 is God’s charge to a person, not reciprocal counsel among peers.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-31:17\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Luqman tells his son to command what is recognized as right, forbid wrong, and be patient through affliction; this is a close practical counterpart to truth and patience, recast in the focus as mutual practice.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"31:17\",\"ar\":\"وَأْمُرْ بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ وَٱنْهَ عَنِ ٱلْمُنكَرِ وَٱصْبِرْ عَلَىٰ مَآ أَصَابَكَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus pairs counsel in الحق with counsel in الصبر.\",\"limits\":\"Luqman addresses his son with individual imperatives; the verse does not use the focus’s reciprocal form or the word الحق.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-31:30\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The next verse names signs for every ṣabbār and grateful person; across this short sequence, divine truth and steadfast reception of signs meet, echoing the focus’s pairing of حق and صبر.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"31:30\",\"ar\":\"أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ هُوَ ٱلْحَقُّ\"},{\"ref\":\"31:31\",\"ar\":\"لَءَايَٰتٍۢ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٍۢ شَكُورٍۢ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus places الحق and الصبر together in its closing counsel pair.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not make patience the content of counsel or explicitly link its two verses as a reciprocal practice.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-31:33\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The family charge in 31:14 is followed later by a warning that no parent can answer for a child on the Day of Judgment; against that limit, the focus’s mutual counsel may describe guidance people can give one another in life, not substitution at judgment.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"31:14\",\"ar\":\"وَوَصَّيْنَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ بِوَٰلِدَيْهِ\"},{\"ref\":\"31:33\",\"ar\":\"لَّا يَجْزِى وَالِدٌ عَن وَلَدِهِۦ وَلَا مَوْلُودٌ هُوَ جَازٍ عَن وَالِدِهِۦ شَيْـًٔا\"}],\"missing\":\"Neither passage explicitly contrasts counsel with intercession. A passage connecting mutual guidance to each person’s final accountability could decide whether this chain illuminates the focus.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-32:18\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The rhetorical question refuses to equate a believer with a transgressor, a compact contrast that reinforces the focus’s distinction between those in loss and its excepted group.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"32:18\",\"ar\":\"أَفَمَن كَانَ مُؤْمِنًۭا كَمَن كَانَ فَاسِقًۭا ۚ لَّا يَسْتَوُۥنَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus likewise defines a distinct group beginning with belief.\",\"limits\":\"This verse does not specify the focus’s righteous deeds or reciprocal practices.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-32:19\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Faith and righteous deeds receive the abode gardens as a reward, followed by a contrasting fate for those who transgress.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"32:19\",\"ar\":\"أَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ فَلَهُمْ جَنَّٰتُ ٱلْمَأْوَىٰ\"}],\"activation\":\"The same pair opens the focus’s excepted category.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not include truth or patience as shared counsel.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-32:24\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Patience is linked here with being made leaders who guide by God’s command, giving endurance a communal guiding consequence alongside the focus’s mutual exhortation to patience.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"32:24\",\"ar\":\"وَجَعَلْنَا مِنْهُمْ أَئِمَّةًۭ يَهْدُونَ بِأَمْرِنَا لَمَّا صَبَرُوا۟\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus makes patience a practice transmitted between members of a group.\",\"limits\":\"The verse attributes leadership to God’s making and does not say those leaders mutually counsel one another.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-33:31\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Within instructions to the Prophet’s wives, a woman’s righteous deed is followed by a promised doubled reward, giving an individually scoped instance of عمل صالح.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"33:31\",\"ar\":\"وَتَعْمَلْ صَٰلِحًۭا نُّؤْتِهَآ أَجْرَهَا مَرَّتَيْنِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s second predicate also concerns righteous action.\",\"limits\":\"This passage addresses a specific household and does not discuss faith’s full profile or mutual counsel.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-33:35\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"This catalogue explicitly names truthful men and women and patient men and women among the rewarded; it expands the focus’s compact communal profile while making women visible in each paired category.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"33:35\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ وَٱلصَّٰدِقَٰتِ وَٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ وَٱلصَّٰبِرَٰتِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus places truth and patience at the close of its group description.\",\"limits\":\"The catalogue names truthful and patient people, not the focus’s exact words الحق or mutual verb تَوَاصَوْا۟.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-33:71\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The sequence puts a command to speak a sound word immediately before God’s promise to set deeds right; it gives the focus’s coupling of truthful counsel and righteous action a concrete speech-and-work counterpart.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"33:70\",\"ar\":\"وَقُولُوا۟ قَوْلًۭا سَدِيدًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"33:71\",\"ar\":\"يُصْلِحْ لَكُمْ أَعْمَٰلَكُمْ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus joins righteous deeds with counsel in truth.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not use reciprocal counsel or mention patience.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-33:72\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The surrounding passage moves from sound speech and corrected deeds to humanity carrying the trust, then distinguishes believers in the outcome; the focus could be heard as a concise profile of responsible human response.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"33:71\",\"ar\":\"يُصْلِحْ لَكُمْ أَعْمَٰلَكُمْ\"},{\"ref\":\"33:72\",\"ar\":\"وَحَمَلَهَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ ۖ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ ظَلُومًۭا جَهُولًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"33:73\",\"ar\":\"وَيَتُوبَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَى ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَٱلْمُؤْمِنَٰتِ\"}],\"missing\":\"The passage does not identify the focus’s loss with the burden of the trust. Another passage connecting accountable trust-bearing to faith, deeds, truth, and patience could secure this reading.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-34:6\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"Those given knowledge recognize the revelation as الحق and as guidance; this could inform what believers pass among themselves as truth, while the verse locates that truth first in revealed guidance.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"34:6\",\"ar\":\"هُوَ ٱلْحَقَّ وَيَهْدِىٓ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطِ ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْحَمِيدِ\"}],\"missing\":\"The wording does not say that the focus’s counsel in الحق is specifically recitation of revelation. A passage joining reciprocal counsel to revealed guidance would decide that identification.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-34:13\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"David’s household is told to make work an act of gratitude, one concrete framing of good action beyond the focus’s otherwise general category.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"34:13\",\"ar\":\"ٱعْمَلُوٓا۟ ءَالَ دَاوُۥدَ شُكْرًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages emphasize action as part of a faithful life.\",\"limits\":\"The command concerns gratitude for a particular favor and does not address mutual truth or patience.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-34:26\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The parties are to be gathered and judged بِٱلْحَقِّ; this may let mutual counsel in truth resonate with truth as the standard by which disputes are finally decided.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"34:26\",\"ar\":\"يَجْمَعُ بَيْنَنَا رَبُّنَا ثُمَّ يَفْتَحُ بَيْنَنَا بِٱلْحَقِّ\"}],\"missing\":\"The verse speaks of divine adjudication, not counsel among believers. Another passage connecting truth-bearing counsel with judgment between disputing parties could establish the relation.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-34:37\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Wealth and children are denied as routes to nearness; the exception is instead belief and righteous action, whose people are secure in the chambers. The verse strips status and lineage from the focus’s profile.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"34:37\",\"ar\":\"وَمَآ أَمْوَٰلُكُمْ وَلَآ أَوْلَٰدُكُم بِٱلَّتِى تُقَرِّبُكُمْ عِندَنَا زُلْفَىٰٓ\"},{\"ref\":\"34:37\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا مَنْ ءَامَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَٰلِحًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"34:37\",\"ar\":\"وَهُمْ فِى ٱلْغُرُفَٰتِ ءَامِنُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The verse repeats the focus’s opening profile and places it against presumed routes to closeness.\",\"limits\":\"Its exception names belief and action but not mutual truth or patience.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-35:7\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The matching faith-and-deeds formula is set against disbelief and paired with forgiveness and a great reward.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"35:7\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ لَهُم مَّغْفِرَةٌۭ وَأَجْرٌۭ كَبِيرٌ\"}],\"activation\":\"These are the focus’s first two conditions.\",\"limits\":\"The contrast and reward add no detail about the focus’s reciprocal practices.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-35:10\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"A good word rises to God and righteous action raises it; this tightly joins word and deed, offering a counterpart to the focus’s move from righteous action to mutual truth-speaking.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"35:10\",\"ar\":\"إِلَيْهِ يَصْعَدُ ٱلْكَلِمُ ٱلطَّيِّبُ وَٱلْعَمَلُ ٱلصَّٰلِحُ يَرْفَعُهُۥ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus combines deeds with truthful speech shared among believers.\",\"limits\":\"The verse says الكلم الطيب, not الحق or تواصوا, and contains no patience clause.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-36:50\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"At the sudden end, people cannot make a tawṣiya; the focus’s reciprocal تَوَاصَوْا۟ can be heard as counsel exchanged while people still have time to act on it.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"36:50\",\"ar\":\"فَلَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ تَوْصِيَةًۭ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus uses a reciprocal form from the same وصي root for an ongoing shared practice.\",\"limits\":\"The forms and settings differ: this is a final bequest prevented by death, not necessarily the same kind of counsel as in 103:3.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:31\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The surrounding exchange gives a failed social relation: one side says it had no authority over the other, and another admits misleading and being misguided. This could serve as a negative counterpart to mutual counsel in truth.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"37:30\",\"ar\":\"وَمَا كَانَ لَنَا عَلَيْكُم مِّن سُلْطَٰنٍۭ ۖ بَلْ كُنتُمْ قَوْمًۭا طَٰغِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"37:31\",\"ar\":\"فَحَقَّ عَلَيْنَا قَوْلُ رَبِّنَآ\"},{\"ref\":\"37:32\",\"ar\":\"فَأَغْوَيْنَٰكُمْ إِنَّا كُنَّا غَٰوِينَ\"}],\"missing\":\"The scene never names truthful mutual counsel as the alternative to mutual misguidance. A passage explicitly contrasting the two social practices could make the link decisive.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:37\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"After opponents call the messenger a mad poet, the answer is that he brought الحق and affirmed the messengers; this sets truthful speech against public ridicule and denial.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"37:36\",\"ar\":\"لِشَاعِرٍۢ مَّجْنُونٍۭ\"},{\"ref\":\"37:37\",\"ar\":\"بَلْ جَآءَ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَصَدَّقَ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus makes truth the message believers are to share with one another.\",\"limits\":\"This is a messenger’s proclamation and its rejection, not a depiction of believers exhorting one another.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:96\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"In the idol-making scene, the assertion that God created people and what they make complicates how human work is described; it could frame the focus’s righteous action within divine creation and human accountability.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"37:95\",\"ar\":\"أَتَعْبُدُونَ مَا تَنْحِتُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"37:96\",\"ar\":\"وَٱللَّهُ خَلَقَكُمْ وَمَا تَعْمَلُونَ\"}],\"missing\":\"The focus says people do righteous deeds but does not raise the question of who creates their acts. Another passage directly relating righteous action to divine creation or human responsibility would be needed.\",\"support\":\"weak\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:100\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"Abraham asks to be granted one “among the righteous”; the shared صالح root may connect the focus’s righteous deeds with membership in a righteous human company, though the forms differ.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"37:100\",\"ar\":\"رَبِّ هَبْ لِى مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ\"}],\"missing\":\"Here الصالحين names persons, while the focus’s الصالحات names deeds. A passage that explicitly relates righteous persons to righteous deeds could establish the proposed class relation.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:112\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Isaac is called a prophet among the righteous, but the shared صالح root names people here and deeds in the focus, so the wording does not specify the focus’s category.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"37:111\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّهُۥ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"37:112\",\"ar\":\"نَبِيًّۭا مِّنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s first predicates likewise identify a group by faith and righteousness.\",\"limits\":\"This names Isaac’s status; it does not describe the reciprocal truth and patience practices in 103:3.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-38:24\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"In a dispute among associates, many wrong one another except those who believe and do righteous deeds—and those are few. The exact exception formula is placed directly against social injustice, while the focus adds truth and patience as communal safeguards.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"38:23\",\"ar\":\"فَقَالَ أَكْفِلْنِيهَا وَعَزَّنِى فِى ٱلْخِطَابِ\"},{\"ref\":\"38:24\",\"ar\":\"وَإِنَّ كَثِيرًۭا مِّنَ ٱلْخُلَطَآءِ لَيَبْغِى بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus repeats the exception phrase and immediately extends it with two practices governing relations among people.\",\"limits\":\"38:24 says this group is few; that qualification is not stated in the focus.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-38:28\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The question refuses to equate believers who do righteous deeds with corrupters on earth; this makes the focus’s moral exception a sharp social distinction rather than a neutral list of traits.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"38:28\",\"ar\":\"أَمْ نَجْعَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ كَٱلْمُفْسِدِينَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus defines its exception through the same belief-and-deeds predicates.\",\"limits\":\"This verse does not state the focus’s truth and patience clauses.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-39:10\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The call to believers places patience after worldly goodness and the breadth of God’s earth, then promises the patient an unmeasured reward; patience is presented as sustained faithfulness with a promised horizon.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"39:10\",\"ar\":\"لِلَّذِينَ أَحْسَنُوا۟ فِى هَٰذِهِ ٱلدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةٌۭ ۗ وَأَرْضُ ٱللَّهِ وَٰسِعَةٌ\"},{\"ref\":\"39:10\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّمَا يُوَفَّى ٱلصَّٰبِرُونَ أَجْرَهُم بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍۢ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus ends its profile with patience as something believers mutually counsel.\",\"limits\":\"39:10 promises reward to the patient but does not describe mutual counsel or name the same exception formula.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}"}}
